        ],
        "text": "According to Ira S. Sacks, the State of New York, as amicus, argued that the Treaty of Buffalo Creek and earlier treaties extinguished Indian title and other Indian possessory rights to the properties at issue long before the Oneida Indian Nation purchased the properties in 1997 and 1998."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "4342e184b148a550591a8a9a0958d37ad7ef118153c08b79fc52b9a50fa79c03",
